  "observations": [
    "Complete registered owner class and attack goal read; live target canUse. Own animation state/LOS/random checks can enqueue hex type2 with200 cooldown, require distance<7 to set spell1 and execute at animation tick36; stop resets cooldown/duration but does not reset enqueuedAttackType. No own direct server guard in attack tick/hex; engine AI scheduler remains outside this study.",
    "hexAttack checks current UUID list size<3, random boolean, then15 candidate sight-clip attempts through findSummonSpot. The core ACMath.getGroundBelowPosition source is absent in the inspected local cache; no safe-floor, bounds, fluid or full-body/collision guarantee. This missing consumer prevents complete-chain credit.",
    "On a candidate, createRandomPossessedMob chooses six registry types at cumulative thresholds .1,.2,.5,.65,.75,1. No create-null guard. If ServerLevel, finalizeSpawn MOB_SUMMONED before owner ID and placement. Request addFreshEntity, then unconditionally record UUID, send event/sound, mark flagtrue. No successful-add transaction, failed-add refund or fallback-on-false. Other spawn initialization chains not fully expanded.",
    "Three Optional<UUID> owner slots are separate from child integer entity ID. getPossessedUUIDs returns nonempty slots without deduplication. add fills first two then sets/overwrites third without own universal capacity/duplicate guard; load calls it for every NBT entry without clearing or limiting the input list. cap3 at hex request is not a proven global population cap.",
    "Owner server tick resolves UUIDs only in current ServerLevel; missing/unloaded entities are not pruned. Resolved member gets owner runtime ID and owner current target before liveness/interface rejection removes UUID. Slots for failed/unloaded joins can continue to block ordinary summoning. No world-wide reconciliation, timer refund or exact ownership proof.",
    "Every owner remove(reason) requests killAllPossessedEntities before super, for any reason. Current loaded resolved members receive magic hurt300; result ignored. No direct discard, guaranteed death, slot clear, child registry cleanup, invulnerability/Forge cancellation composition or cross-dimension cleanup demonstrated. This is a damage cleanup request, including nondeath removal reasons, not atomic member deletion.",
    "Owner serializes list of UUIDs as Possessed. Interface resolves child integer ID to any Licowitch in same Level without UUID/alive check; particle helper separately tests owneralive. Shown child own save/read methods in Candicorn, GummyBear, Gumbeeper, CaramelCube and Gingerbread do not explicitly encode owner ID. Complete inherited serializer/capability/reload order not read, so no universal reload-loss or entity-ID reuse exploit claim.",
    "Candicorn defines child owner ID default0; the inspected five other member defaults use-1. Explicit shouldDropLoot gates on Candicorn/GummyBear/CaramelCube/Gingerbread/Caniac require ID==-1 and delegate. Gumbeeper inspected own data/target/custom-death methods do not establish the same loot gate. No universal no-loot, XP, equipment, actual item drop or material pickup guarantee.",
    "CaramelCube finalize randomizes size0..2. Its removal on server, size>0 and dead/dying attempts smaller children before super; copied fields are persistence flag, name,noAI,invulnerability,size/health,position/yaw, without explicit owner ID/owner UUID enrollment. Own default child ID is-1. Adds unchecked. Conditional untracked descendants are a source-level boundary, not reproduced material farming, actual population gain or credit for an extra splitting family.",
    "canAttack delegates after owner-friendly filter in inspected six member snippets. Caniac arm AOE has an additional return for a friendly entity, which exits the whole shown loop rather than continuing. Target assignment/friendly checks are supporting context, not proof of every attack/AI path or client feedback.",
    "The summon cohort is structurally distinct from EA10 hive storage commit-on-add, EA11 rider-delay expiry and EA16 alarm once-attempt latch; those complete prior decision fields actually read, but whole old source chains not reread. EA19 cohort transfer comparison reuses already-read full formal decision from same active turn. Missing ground/consumer/native entry closure means this record remains0 despite possible semantic distinction."
  ],
